<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10486" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conserva</span></b> , ae, f.
		conservus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a (female) fellow-slave.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas.
				1, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Mil. 4, 8, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun.
				2, 3, 75</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 17, 5 al.</span></i>; <i>dat. plur.</i> conservabus, <i><span class="en">Dig. 33,
				7, 27</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b> to inanimate things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nolo ego foris conservas Meas a te verberarier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					As. 2, 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">duraque conservae ligna, valete, fores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 1, 6, 74</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
